apture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n2{x}_{3}=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}+3(2)=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=6-7=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5(-1)+(2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1+5-2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha