" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+y-z=2 \\\\  & y+3z=6 \\\\  & -z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=-3\\,⟹\\,z=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=6\\,⟹\\,y=6-9=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-3$ into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n2x+(-3)-(3)=2\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(2+3+3)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=-3$ and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨4,-3,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cdfdf77afed68f2fd83e2d020aaa86c88f0c78a077b8cecf978986f1be51d25c" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,-3,3⟩"] "category" "ma_capture"