_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,-3,3⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/state.json" "file_sha256" "c214e034109a4d35a776f90289590cb5ec56b86ce4f2b3ad3b814645b045b53f" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=3 \\\\ y+z=2 \\\\ z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4690.json" "file_sha256" "04b85d770b91ec8aecaa9f9591c597fafa61808689376b883f66d7a0a5a3fd04" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 2-2 = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = 3-2 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1,$ $y=0,$ and $z = 2.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4690.json" "file_sha256" "04b85d770b91ec8aecaa9f9591c597fafa61808689376b883f66d7a0a5a3fd04" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4691.json" "file_sha256" "6b0ff4079b242844a8429613fc2c1c14900c9b9b4f030f25f29b4a1d588af9a8" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4691.json" "file_sha256" "6b0ff4079b242844a8429613fc2c1c14900c9b9b4f030f25f29b4a1d588af9a8" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4692.json" "file_sha256" "1549c393295f8019c940b9e6aa0375aa99f6b9f8d4957cef1bba7ee697973be8" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/example-4692.json" "file_sha256" "1549c393295f8019c940b9e6aa0375aa99f6b9f8d4957cef1bba7ee697973be8" "basis" 1400 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14039987/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-129447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(\\frac{1}{2})+(-1)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2+1+1=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=4$, ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}$, and ${x}_{3}=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨4,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-129447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,-\\frac{3}{2},-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,-\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,-\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129447" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=3.$ Substitute this into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-(3)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1+3=2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(2)+(3)=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1-3+2=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=0$,  ${x}_{2}=2$, and ${x}_{3}=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,2,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10196" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-10196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,2,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,3,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-3,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-3,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,3,2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10196" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,2,3⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y-z=4 \\\\  & y+2z=2 \\\\  & z=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "he third equation states that  $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(\\frac{1}{2})=2\\,⟹\\,y=2-1=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $y=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx-(1)-(\\frac{1}{2})=4\\,⟹\\,x=4+1+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{11}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{2}$,  $y=1$, and $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨\\frac{11}{2},1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-10197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,\\frac{9}{2},-\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{11}{2},1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{2},-1,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{9}{2},1,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{9}{2},2,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{11}{2},1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}=3 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6(-\\frac{1}{3})=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3-2=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+1-(-\\frac{1}{3})=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2-1-\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{3}$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129455" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-129455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129455" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" 