solution can be written as $⟨11,3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-10198" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10198" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨11,3,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨11,3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨12,-3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨9,-3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨9,2,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10198" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨11,3,\\frac{1}{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=5 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(2)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(-2)+4(2)=5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=5-6-8=-9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=-9$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-9,-2,2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20422" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-20422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-3,-1,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-9,-2,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-8,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,0,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨8,1,2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20422" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-9,-2,2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that  ${x}_{3}=-3.$ Substituting this into the second equation,  we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(-3)=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2-2(-3)=-2+6=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(4)+3(-3)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1-8+9=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=0$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=-3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n$[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-20452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-20452" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+3z=-2 \\\\  & y+4z=0 \\\\  & z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+4(3)=0\\,⟹\\,y=-12.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-12$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-12)+3(3)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-2+12-9=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=1$, $y=-12$, and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨1,-12,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,-12,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨-22,-12,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨-22,12,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-12,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,12,3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129459" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,-12,3⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{3} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=2 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+\\frac{{x}_{3}}{3}=-1 \\\\  & {x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+\\frac{2}{3}=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1-\\frac{2}{3}=-\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{3}$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3(-\\frac{5}{3})+(2)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2+5-2=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=5$, ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{3}$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨5,-\\frac{5}{3},2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129457" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-129457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{3},2⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\frac{1}{3},2⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,-\\frac{5}{3},2⟩"] ["math" "⟨5,-\\frac{1}{3},2⟩"] ["math" "⟨5,-\\frac{5}{3},2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129457" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨5,-\\frac{5}{3},2⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=1 \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=0$, and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,0,1⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10205" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-10205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,0,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,1,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,1,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,0,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,1,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-10205" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,0,1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7 \\\\  & 2{x}_{3}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n2{x}_{3}=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}+3(2)=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=6-7=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5(-1)+(2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1+5-2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-30 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129615" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+y-z=2 \\\\  & y+3z=6 \\\\  & -z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=-3\\,⟹\\,z=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=6\\,⟹\\,y=6-9=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-3$ into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n2x+(-3)-(3)=2\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(2+3+3)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=-3$ and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨4,-3,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨1,-3,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,3,-3⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,-4,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,4,-3⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,-3,3⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72980" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,-3,3⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 4x+y+2z=-3 \\\\  & y+3z=0 \\\\  & -z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=1\\,⟹\\,z=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(-1)=0\\,⟹\\,y=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-1$ and $y=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n4x+(3)+2(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{-3-3+2}{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1$, $y=3$, and $z=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as \n$[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129604" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-129604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]."] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]."] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]."] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129604" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\  & -{x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n-{x}_{3}=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{3}=1.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-3-2=-5.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=-5$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}-(-5)+4(1)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{-1-5-4}{2}=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=-5$, ${x}_{2}=-5$, and ${x}_{3}=1.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-129613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-129613" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+y+z=-1 \\\\  & y+z=1 \\\\  & 2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n \n\n$$\n2z=1\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(\\frac{1}{2})=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=y=\\frac{1}{2}$  into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x+(\\frac{1}{2})+(\\frac{1}{2})=-1\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(-1-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1$, $y=\\frac{1}{2}$, and $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a6fbec75967a5925a5e6bc423e61d8d4adc15a7cdb910e039347daf9f9d1dbc9"} {"question" "q-72983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,-1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\frac{1}{2},1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "q-72983" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/state.json" "file_sha256" "c291ffb31426989ca32cb4709dfec1a3548871ec37e4a88d3317f906e7b2008e"} {"question" "e-4690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the following system of equations:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/3b7ca238880ce9b06f58b1667d29b3fa0103560fa475238134cd3e802c7e7720.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/example-4690.json" "file_sha256" "d098b775db7cf348922ecc34470dddcc8442f923aa73a651ae3af7d23e79342c"} {"question" "e-4690" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The third equation states that $z=2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(2)=2 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\ty = 2-2 = 0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $z=2$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(2)=3\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx = 3-2 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x = 1,$ $y=0,$ and $z = 2.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 1,0,2 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/example-4690.json" "file_sha256" "d098b775db7cf348922ecc34470dddcc8442f923aa73a651ae3af7d23e79342c"} {"question" "e-4691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/1ecadec01586fecee4a8b6d8ad5015168387124430849ed2e7d884908e28e927.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/example-4691.json" "file_sha256" "5d98967af7a252624f75d95795f3fa186466157ac343c50f1dbe6fb165d613ad"} {"question" "e-4691" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/c7c7d0904aa85c2cd9915e95a8ca3cee9857deb216148f59372204c6672d8811.png)\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/example-4691.json" "file_sha256" "5d98967af7a252624f75d95795f3fa186466157ac343c50f1dbe6fb165d613ad"} {"question" "e-4692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/fd5c0fe6de60e36b0bd2414cb8ef991265c30bdfa4d8cfdac3242f51a54dbb87.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/example-4692.json" "file_sha256" "fa513daf43e1008b9d2f0ea0bc9fa4997c6a5da148e3cf3750606e81a7fc382f"} {"question" "e-4692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/assets/41347eb5694181e386cae05a31e455d12e2fbd1a0d70cd36bb37ed72da75f82d.png)\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071689/example-4692.json" "file_sha256" "fa513daf43e1008b9d2f0ea0bc9fa4997c6a5da148e3cf3750606e81a7fc382f"}] "usage" {"q-129615" [] "e-4690" [] "q-20422" [] "q-129459" [] "q-72980" [] "q-10205" [] "e-4692" [] "e-4691" []} "basis" 2576 "retractions" [[17592186097097 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186096844 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186096379 :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=3 \\\\ y+z=2 \\\\ z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096380 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096380 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$"] [17592186096381 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096381 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{3}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186093472 17592186093473 17592186093474 17592186093475 17592186093476 17592186094989 17592186094990 17592186094991 17592186094992 17592186094993 17592186304955 17592186304956 17592186304957 17592186304958 17592186304959 17592186304976 17592186304977 17592186304978 17592186304979 17592186304980 17592186304997 17592186304998 17592186304999 17592186305000 17